# --- Rust ---------------------------------------------------------------------
/target
**/*.rs.bk
# NOTE: Cargo.lock IS committed on purpose — this workspace produces binaries
# (floptle-editor, floptle-runtime), so a locked dependency set is reproducible.

# --- Editor / OS scratch ------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/

# Machine-specific cargo config: this repo lives on an NTFS (ntfs3) disk whose
# truncate path deadlocks under concurrent Rust-build I/O, so target-dir is
# redirected to a native-fs path that differs per machine. Keep it out of git.
.cargo/config.toml

# Throwaway dev screenshots / capture shares (not engine content).
/Screenshots/

# CI-built engine binaries consumed by File ⏵ Export Game… (macOS — see
# .github/workflows/macos-binary.yml + docs/export-builds.md). Machine-local.
/prebuilt/

# --- TEMPORARY / LEGALLY-SENSITIVE TEST ASSETS --------------------------------
# Ocarina of Time textures are used ONLY as local placeholder test assets during
# development. They MUST NOT enter git history (we plan to open-source later, and
# scrubbing history is painful). Drop them under assets/textures/_oot_temp/.
# They are git-ignored on purpose; replace with original Fopull textures before
# any public release.
assets/textures/_oot_temp/
assets/**/_oot_temp/

# Third-party / sample test models (e.g. Khronos glTF samples) used to exercise
# the importer during development — kept out of history like the OoT textures.
# Your own models live elsewhere under assets/models/ and ARE committed.
assets/models/_test/

# Large / generated binary assets (imported glTF caches, baked data, etc.)
assets/.cache/
*.blend1
out.png

# Terrain fields are STREAMING DATA, not source:
# bodies carry a genspec in the scene and (re)generate deterministically on
# approach; player edits persist in game SAVE SLOTS (terrain.saveDir), and the
# editor's local project files stay on disk — none of it belongs in git history
# (a single field can exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit).
*.cfield
*.tfield
**/terrain/*.meta

# Player save slots (per-slot save stores + slot terrain caches) — runtime data.
**/saves/

# Crash-recovery autosaves.
**/.floptle/autosave/

# A PROJECT's runtime dirs, for every project in the repo rather than a named
# one. These are written by the engine while the game runs, not authored:
#   save/     — the script save API's slots (floptle_script::save → <project>/save/<slot>.ron)
#   replays/  — recorded rollback match logs (crate::shadow), which get large
# Anchored one level down on purpose. A NESTED folder called `save` is content
# and ships — the same distinction the exporter draws when it decides what a
# build carries.
/*/save/
/*/replays/

# Auto-seeded UI effect examples in the scratch/default project (regenerated on
# project open; the canonical copies live under each real project, e.g. solar/).
assets/shaders/examples/ui/

# A PROJECT's package registry. `Source::Linked` records an ABSOLUTE path on the
# machine that linked it — "/home/someone/…" — so this file is developer state,
# not project source: committing it hands everyone else a path that exists on
# exactly one computer. Anchored one level down like the runtime dirs above, so
# it covers every project in the repo without naming one.
/*/packages.ron

# Offscreen render-probe outputs (ui_shader_probe, etc.)
*_probe.png

# --- Agent / tooling scratch --------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code's per-project state (session transcripts, local settings). Machine-
# and person-specific, and it can carry conversation content — never in history.
.claude/

# --- Internal working material (local only) -----------------------------------
# Working notes: handoffs, proposals for unshipped systems, roadmaps, and the
# decision records behind them. They are drafts and intentions rather than
# documentation of the engine, and docs/ is the shipped surface. Kept on disk,
# out of the repo.
/.internal/
/CLAUDE.md

# Python bytecode from the repo's helper scripts (solar/tools/…). Regenerated on
# every run and interpreter-version-specific, so it is pure churn in a diff.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Local packaging output (scripts/package.sh writes bundles + releases.json here;
# real releases are built by CI and published to GitHub Releases).
/dist/
/builds/
builds.zip

# Source-art archives dropped at the repo root while working (texture/VFX packs
# and the like). They are INPUTS to the assets under assets/ and each is tens of
# megabytes — the same call as builds.zip above. Unpacked art that the engine
# actually loads is committed; the archive it came out of is not.
/*.zip

# --- Dev capture scratch ------------------------------------------------------
# Ad-hoc screenshots and render probes people drop at the repo root while
# debugging. The named *_probe.png rule above only catches the ones that follow
# the convention; these are the rest.
/*.png
!/docs/**/*.png

# The two release binaries and per-run JSON that scripts/scene-bench.sh builds
# to compare script VMs. Each binary is the whole editor; the numbers that
# matter out of a run are recorded in the plan doc by hand, not committed here.
/.bench/
